'c' is "chat" in NetHack 4, but tries to operate as "close" in some
circumstances for keystroke compatibility with 3.4.3 ("close" is on 'o'
in NetHack 4, like "open" is). There are a few cases where the game gets
chatting and closing muddled, as a result.

I've mentioned this problem on the relevant bug ticket
(http://trac.nethack4.org/ticket/118), so that we don't forget it.

